.@_sholtodouglas and @DarioAmodei are right to be con concerned about AI driving an increase in the concentration of economic power.  

@zhitzig and I write about the forces toward and against centralization in "AI's Use of Knowledge in Society,"  https://t.co/vEsgIPqIHh 

I discuss some alternative approaches in The Turing Trap: https://t.co/l7jMNeF3ra

@lens2645211 @GavinSBaker @_sholtodouglas That's my point.
Notions of Good and Bad are in the eye of the beholder. 
Hence we need a wide diversity of AI assistants/agents, or else the dominant supplier will decide what's good or bad.

@ns123abc I too hate OpenAI, but I don’t *enjoy* doing so. 

It just reflects a specific pattern of behavior that I have been observing and documenting for seven years. 

It is what it is.  They are who they are.

